 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. Advertised standard variable rates from the big banks have been about 0.58 percentage points higher for investors than for owner-occupiers.\n\n- **Owner-occupier standard variable:** 8.77% a year in September 2026 (the latest month available)\n- **Investor standard variable:** 9.35% a year in September 2026\n\nThe gap has been 0.58 points in every month since January 2024, even though both rates moved together. For example, both were cut to 8.02% and 8.60% in August 2025, and both rose again in February to May 2026.\n\nThese are advertised (headline) rates from RBA table F5. The RBA notes that rates actually paid on new loans are lower, especially for borrowers who negotiate discounts. I didn't check the actual paid rates, which are in table F6, so I can't say whether the gap is the same for those.",
